{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of terms in an A.P. (Arithmetic Progression) is even. The sum of the odd and even-numbered terms are 24 and 30, respectively. If the last term exceeds the first by 10.5, the number of terms in the A.P. is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea40b84bf2828fc989191ce9a27ea28781e0c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 18 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 10 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the first term, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of terms, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the common difference.  That means the last term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a592e8e42ededf9ff3f183e4243240b11977a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+r(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can write an equation on the difference between the last and first term based on the conditions.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/7/da7bdd32e4a6d1891a738bf21193b0507ff7c875.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+r(n-1)-a =10.5\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9517449098c2642632aade9ecb3da241188577.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[rn-r=10.5\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />\nAlso, half of the terms add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> while the other half of the terms add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a67ce472a92be25324ee855bd22383ccfc98f63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24 + r\\frac{n}{2} = 30\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcdb3344e4903631ee9812d42e4ade66c9b8e133.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[nr = 12\\]\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />\nSubstituting the value back to a previous equation,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52cad9c79265474af58dd28b7d21a8327668e06c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12-r=10.5\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/15225a3402a68b83ca1f39fbe5a9d4a06fee9153.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=1.5\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />\nSubstituting to a previous equation again,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c37ac592620b5539040f6183d329186b5d005a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1.5n-1.5=10.5\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/a/2ba83bf8758acefe099680e230795f472acecdae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=8\\]\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />\nThus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d724db96e8cb75176d053467614c78aca041470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" /> terms in the arithmetic sequence.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"